cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "Cardscape"
type: software
date-released: 2026-07-27
url: "https://cardscape.fitty.ar"
repository-code: "https://github.com/cardscape/cardscape"
license: RPL-1.5
keywords:
  - kanban
  - project-management
  - self-hosted
  - self-hostable
  - mcp
  - model-context-protocol
  - ai
  - dotnet
  - blazor
  - entity-framework
  - open-source
abstract: >-
  Cardscape is an open-source, self-hostable kanban and
  project-management tool with a first-class Model Context
  Protocol (MCP) server. Built on .NET 10 (LTS), it
  persists to SQLite, PostgreSQL, or MariaDB and is
  licensed under RPL-1.5. The MCP server is the
  differentiator: it lets any AI-compatible client
  (Claude Desktop, Cursor, Windsurf, etc.) read and drive
  the boards through the same Application layer the REST
  API uses.
